e distinct 2\u2011adic exponents and the odd factor \\(r^{2^{k}m}\\) is coprime to the power of two.  Since \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are both multiples of \\(2^{k}\\) and \\(k\\ge2\\),\n\n\\[\n\\min(A,B)\\ge2^{k}\\ge k+2.\n\\]\n\nHence \\(2^{k+2}\\mid b^{a}-f(b)^{\\,f(a)}\\).\n\nAll possibilities for \\((a,b)\\) have been covered, so the function (9) is bonza.\n\nFor a power of two \\(n=2^{k}\\) with \\(k\\ge2\\) we have \\(f(n)=2^{k+2}=4n\\); thus the ratio \\(f(n)/n\\) attains the value \\(4\\).  Consequently the constant \\(4\\) cannot be lowered.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 6. Conclusion\n\nEvery bonza function satisfies \\(f(n)\\le4n\\) for all positive integers \\(n\\), and the function defined in (9) shows that the factor \\(4\\) is best possible.  Hence the smallest real constant with the required property is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}.\n\\]"
